WEBVTT

00:01.335 --> 00:03.337
[♪ theme music playing]

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.826
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:37.037 --> 00:39.039
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

00:53.553 --> 00:54.680
[breathing shakily]

01:35.012 --> 01:37.806
But why would you say liking me

01:38.849 --> 01:40.517
is being greedy?

01:41.101 --> 01:42.603
Because you'll go back soon?

01:43.395 --> 01:45.439
It doesn't matter if I'm being greedy now.

01:47.899 --> 01:49.568
I can't stop my feelings anyway.

01:52.612 --> 01:54.156
So I'll just keep going,

01:54.239 --> 01:56.783
because I don't want
to waste our time together.

01:59.619 --> 02:02.622
Then don't say
you're being greedy anymore.

02:03.165 --> 02:04.458
If you say that again,

02:05.375 --> 02:06.793
I won't let it slide.

02:08.253 --> 02:09.629
I should be careful, then.

02:10.255 --> 02:11.298
[chuckles softly]

02:13.383 --> 02:14.384
[♪ song fades]

02:14.468 --> 02:16.261
EPISODE 8

02:18.138 --> 02:19.973
Stop staring at it.

02:20.057 --> 02:21.850
It won't even be visible tomorrow.

02:23.268 --> 02:25.979
Oh. And make sure to call your grandma.

02:26.063 --> 02:28.440
She'll be worried sick
after you left like that.

02:29.524 --> 02:31.610
[inhales sharply] I will.

02:34.655 --> 02:36.531
I used to be just like that watch.

02:37.991 --> 02:41.995
I was frozen in time,
but someone made time move again for me.

02:42.621 --> 02:43.705
Like this.

02:49.252 --> 02:53.799
So how about letting time with your dad
start moving again?

02:58.428 --> 03:00.097
The past is the past.

03:00.639 --> 03:01.682
What's important

03:02.766 --> 03:04.476
is the time that will flow from now on.

03:15.070 --> 03:17.322
[♪ pleasant music playing]

03:27.290 --> 03:29.501
[Nana] Her boyfriend died back then.

03:29.584 --> 03:32.587
He went to study in Boston,
but he suddenly died.

03:32.671 --> 03:33.797
Hey, roomie.

03:33.880 --> 03:37.801
[Chan] The fact that I lived
while he died from that accident…

03:38.635 --> 03:40.220
It's a good thing you took it out.

03:41.096 --> 03:44.433
I want someone to have joy in their life.

03:44.516 --> 03:48.061
She was a grateful disruption
that made me live again.

03:51.898 --> 03:53.525
Mr. Park, we…

03:54.276 --> 03:56.361
Of course. I know.

04:04.786 --> 04:06.329
Take her home safely.

04:07.873 --> 04:10.000
Let's go, Genius.

04:30.937 --> 04:31.938
Go on in.

04:34.816 --> 04:35.942
Bye.

04:36.026 --> 04:37.027
[♪ music fades]

04:38.445 --> 04:40.530
[Haran stutters] Look forward.

04:40.614 --> 04:42.616
It'll be dangerous
if you fall down the hill.

04:42.699 --> 04:44.659
[♪ pleasant music continues]

04:48.538 --> 04:50.081
[sighs] I'm relieved.

04:51.249 --> 04:52.250
You're warm.

04:53.126 --> 04:54.544
It's just that…

04:55.670 --> 04:56.880
this feels like a dream.

04:58.381 --> 04:59.800
I can't believe it.

05:09.100 --> 05:10.685
-Should I make this feel more real?
-[grunts]

05:10.769 --> 05:12.062
No, thanks.

05:12.145 --> 05:13.146
[both laugh]

05:13.897 --> 05:15.732
[sighs] I'll go now. Head inside.

05:16.316 --> 05:17.359
Get back safely.

05:34.417 --> 05:35.418
[♪ music ends]

05:35.502 --> 05:36.545
What a relief.

05:40.215 --> 05:41.216
[grunts]

05:42.551 --> 05:43.552
[groans]

05:44.219 --> 05:45.679
-[groans softly]
-[door opens]

05:45.762 --> 05:48.181
[Chan] Now, now.

05:48.265 --> 05:50.475
You didn't take your meds again? [grunts]

05:52.060 --> 05:54.980
-I told you to take them on time.
-[sighs]

05:55.063 --> 05:57.607
Let's go to the hospital this week.

05:57.691 --> 06:01.278
Keep your cardiac enzyme
test results in your wallet

06:02.153 --> 06:05.699
so someone can see it if you ever collapse
when you're not with me.

06:06.324 --> 06:07.325
We have to go, okay?

06:07.951 --> 06:11.204
Just think of me as a nagging son,

06:11.288 --> 06:13.373
and come with me.

06:14.291 --> 06:15.542
All right.

06:15.625 --> 06:16.751
And you

06:17.419 --> 06:20.130
should think of me
as a father who listens to you,

06:20.755 --> 06:22.591
so tell me anything

06:23.550 --> 06:25.844
that you have a hard time
telling anyone else.

06:25.927 --> 06:28.054
You can tell me
anything that troubles you.

06:29.806 --> 06:31.725
I'll be your safe space.

06:34.603 --> 06:37.522
I wasn't trying to hide
my relationship with Ms. Song…

06:37.606 --> 06:39.024
You really like her, right?

06:39.900 --> 06:41.067
[sighs softly]

06:41.151 --> 06:43.445
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

06:43.528 --> 06:45.155
-Yes.
-All right.

06:45.989 --> 06:50.327
Let her feel joy again.

06:50.410 --> 06:55.206
You don't need a reason
to want someone to be happy.

06:55.290 --> 06:58.668
As long as you're sincere, it's okay.

07:05.925 --> 07:07.969
[deliveryman] Ms. Song,
there's an international delivery.

07:13.975 --> 07:14.976
[Haran] Wow.

07:17.020 --> 07:19.356
I finally got the sketch sample
for my design.

07:19.439 --> 07:20.690
Make some noise!

07:23.276 --> 07:24.861
It's all thanks to this pen.

07:35.914 --> 07:38.792
But how did you come up
with the idea of sending me a pen?

07:41.836 --> 07:45.256
[Chan] I kept thinking about how you said
you felt like you were trapped.

07:48.551 --> 07:50.095
I used to feel that way, too.

07:51.262 --> 07:54.474
Back then, I kept thinking the same thing.

08:00.105 --> 08:01.398
If…

08:02.065 --> 08:04.901
there was just a small crack
to breathe through, I could live.

08:06.569 --> 08:07.570
But…

08:08.071 --> 08:11.074
that "if" never came true for me.

08:12.450 --> 08:14.244
I guess I wanted

08:14.327 --> 08:16.496
that pen to be that "if" for you.

08:17.247 --> 08:18.248
[sighs]

08:19.040 --> 08:21.459
Chan understands me so well…

08:23.336 --> 08:25.672
[Chan] Sorry, I was rambling.

08:26.881 --> 08:28.091
I should go now.

08:37.475 --> 08:38.476
[♪ music fades]

08:39.060 --> 08:40.854
-[Ben] Great work today.
-[Chan] You too.

08:41.938 --> 08:44.232
-I'm going back to Korea first.
-Okay, sure.

08:44.315 --> 08:45.316
[Ben chuckles]

08:46.776 --> 08:48.945
[chuckles, inhales sharply]

08:50.488 --> 08:51.531
[sighs]

08:54.242 --> 08:57.370
[Haran] Maybe it's because I lost
the pen I used for seven years,

08:57.454 --> 09:00.081
but I couldn't sketch anything
during the two days here.

09:01.041 --> 09:03.710
[Chan in English]
Yes, seven years ago. Early July.

09:03.793 --> 09:05.962
And the engraving is Haran.

09:06.046 --> 09:07.255
[shop owner] One second.

09:07.338 --> 09:11.509
Uh, yeah. We have the model name
and the engraving design on file.

09:15.138 --> 09:16.347
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

09:16.431 --> 09:17.474
[Haran sighs]

09:23.354 --> 09:24.939
[in Korean] The past is the past.

09:26.024 --> 09:27.400
What's important…

09:33.198 --> 09:35.158
[Chan and Haran] is the time
that will flow from now on.

09:36.201 --> 09:37.869
[wind whooshing]

09:37.952 --> 09:41.122
-[leaves rustling]
-[birds chirping]

09:41.206 --> 09:43.124
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

09:45.543 --> 09:46.628
[Hayeong] Grandma.

09:46.711 --> 09:47.879
[♪ music fades]

09:47.962 --> 09:49.964
Where have you been?

09:50.048 --> 09:51.716
I was at a meeting.

09:51.800 --> 09:53.176
Our dinner ended late.

09:53.259 --> 09:54.886
A meeting dressed like this?

09:55.720 --> 09:57.138
And what's this…

09:57.222 --> 09:58.264
I'll do it.

09:58.807 --> 10:00.517
I'm tired. I'm going to bed.

10:01.893 --> 10:03.394
Grandma, did you go to Seongsu…

10:03.478 --> 10:05.814
I'm sorry, but just let this go for now.

10:05.897 --> 10:07.023
Please.

10:08.817 --> 10:09.859
What?

10:10.902 --> 10:12.112
I just…

10:12.195 --> 10:15.698
thought we haven't been
talking much lately.

10:15.782 --> 10:18.159
Are you sure nothing's wrong?

10:18.785 --> 10:21.579
What's wrong is you asking questions
when I'm so sleepy.

10:21.663 --> 10:23.206
-[chuckles]
-Go to bed.

10:23.873 --> 10:26.126
All right. Good night.

10:31.131 --> 10:32.423
[♪ pensive music playing]

10:32.507 --> 10:33.925
Why are her shoes like that?

10:35.885 --> 10:37.428
It couldn't have been a meeting.

10:40.056 --> 10:41.558
Where in the world was she?

10:42.183 --> 10:43.268
[sighs wearily]

10:54.320 --> 10:57.407
EXAMINATION

11:16.718 --> 11:17.719
[♪ music fades]

11:17.802 --> 11:19.262
[automation] The door is closing.

11:20.013 --> 11:21.931
[exclaims] Let me get on!

11:22.015 --> 11:23.433
Thank you.

11:23.516 --> 11:26.394
[Hayeong panting]

11:26.477 --> 11:28.104
-[exclaims softly]
-[clears throat]

11:34.235 --> 11:35.361
[Hayeong] What's that?

11:35.445 --> 11:38.281
He's the definition of neatness,
and he's got bedhead?

11:38.364 --> 11:40.700
[in English] Okay,
I'll check and email you.

11:42.368 --> 11:45.079
[♪ whimsical music playing]

11:47.790 --> 11:50.668
[in Korean]
He's late and has bedhead? Mr. Yeon?

11:51.836 --> 11:54.297
What's going on?
That doesn't suit him at all.

11:54.380 --> 11:55.381
[♪ music fades]

11:55.465 --> 11:57.008
-Look. Isn't it crazy?
-[Sol and Raemee exclaim]

11:57.091 --> 11:58.676
-This is insane.
-Is this for real?

11:58.760 --> 12:00.220
Sorry! What are you up to?

12:00.303 --> 12:02.972
Hayeong! Seunggyu took a rare photo.

12:03.056 --> 12:04.349
What photo?

12:04.432 --> 12:07.352
[Seunggyu] I was organizing the photos
I took during my trend research…

12:07.435 --> 12:09.395
[exclaims] and I was shocked.

12:09.479 --> 12:11.773
That stiff, uptight Mr. Yeon is dating?

12:12.482 --> 12:15.944
-This is crazy!
-[Sol and Raemee giggle]

12:16.027 --> 12:18.571
[Sol exclaims delightedly]
But they look so good together.

12:18.655 --> 12:19.656
[Raemee] They do.

12:19.739 --> 12:21.574
-[♪ amusing music playing]
-[folders thud loudly]

12:21.658 --> 12:22.742
How shameless.

12:23.451 --> 12:25.328
Why is she being so loud when she's late?

12:25.411 --> 12:27.622
Hey, look.

12:30.917 --> 12:32.669
She's the head of La Mode Eclat,

12:33.253 --> 12:35.880
-and that's the co-head and her husband.
-[♪ music ends]

12:35.964 --> 12:38.091
-[Sol groans]
-[Raemee] Oh, geez.

12:38.174 --> 12:40.802
Seunggyu! They were just having
a business meeting.

12:40.885 --> 12:44.430
[sighs] So they were the heads
of La Mode Eclat.

12:44.514 --> 12:46.474
[Seunggyu laughs]

12:46.557 --> 12:49.143
-Sorry about that.
-[whistling]

12:51.271 --> 12:53.481
Oh, dear. Why is she suddenly whistling?

12:53.564 --> 12:55.108
There's no in-between with her.

12:55.191 --> 12:56.359
-[Sol chuckles softly]
-[stops whistling]

12:56.859 --> 12:57.860
He's right.

12:58.528 --> 12:59.821
Why am I relieved?

13:00.780 --> 13:01.990
[Seunggyu] But I wonder if Mr. Yeon

13:02.073 --> 13:04.617
would still have that default expression
when he's dating.

13:04.701 --> 13:06.995
[Sol] No way. I'm sure he'll be different.

13:07.078 --> 13:11.791
[inhales sharply] He might be
really sweet to the woman he likes.

13:12.375 --> 13:14.335
[in English] Sweet?

13:14.419 --> 13:16.421
[♪ enchanting music playing]

13:22.510 --> 13:23.511
[in Korean] Your hand.

13:23.594 --> 13:25.555
[Taeseok] You might slip
since you're wearing heels.

13:28.725 --> 13:32.312
-[♪ enchanting music continuing]
-This happened to my friend,

13:32.395 --> 13:33.479
uh…

13:33.563 --> 13:35.815
but this guy

13:35.898 --> 13:39.986
brushed off dry leaves in the dirt
with his bare hands so she wouldn't slip.

13:40.069 --> 13:41.696
What does that mean?

13:41.779 --> 13:42.947
With his bare hands?

13:43.531 --> 13:44.532
That's love.

13:44.615 --> 13:45.783
[stutters] Love?

13:46.701 --> 13:49.912
Then if the woman cried,

13:49.996 --> 13:53.249
and he looked at her with pity
and wiped her tears with his hand,

13:53.332 --> 13:55.126
what does that mean?

13:55.209 --> 13:56.836
[exclaims softly]

13:56.919 --> 13:57.920
[softly] Love.

13:58.004 --> 13:59.839
-[Hayeong gasps] He loves me?
-[♪ amusing music playing]

13:59.922 --> 14:02.550
And the fact that
you're overanalyzing his every move

14:02.633 --> 14:04.510
means you like him too.

14:04.594 --> 14:06.554
-[all exclaim teasingly]
-No, that wasn't about me.

14:06.637 --> 14:07.847
That was my friend.

14:07.930 --> 14:09.307
-It's obvious it was about you.
-[laughs]

14:09.390 --> 14:12.060
My friend told me during a school reunion.

14:12.143 --> 14:13.144
[Sol] You liar.

14:13.227 --> 14:14.270
Ms. Song Hayeong.

14:16.064 --> 14:17.982
-The new material you mentioned…
-[Hayeong] Ah.

14:18.066 --> 14:20.151
Uh… Mmm…

14:23.529 --> 14:24.781
Hello?

14:24.864 --> 14:26.449
Yes, hello.

14:26.532 --> 14:28.993
-I just got an urgent call.
-[♪ music ends]

14:29.077 --> 14:30.536
Are you busy right now?

14:30.620 --> 14:31.621
I'm busy too.

14:32.288 --> 14:34.248
[birds chirping]

14:38.044 --> 14:39.962
What should I say when I give this to her?

14:48.387 --> 14:49.472
Hmm? [chuckles softly]

14:53.768 --> 14:56.229
Hey, you said
you're coming in the evening.

14:56.896 --> 14:58.189
I'm meeting someone here.

14:58.272 --> 14:59.816
Goodness.

14:59.899 --> 15:01.109
You mean with me?

15:01.192 --> 15:02.652
[footsteps approaching rapidly]

15:02.735 --> 15:04.237
-She's meeting me!
-[Chan groans]

15:04.320 --> 15:07.490
-Hmm?
-What? This is so sudden.

15:07.573 --> 15:09.992
Something came up,
so she's returning to Mungyeong today.

15:10.076 --> 15:12.495
Wow. You were going to meet without me?

15:12.995 --> 15:14.831
-You're always leaving me out.
-[Chan's grandma] Right.

15:14.914 --> 15:16.874
[Chan sighs, mumbles playfully]

15:16.958 --> 15:18.626
-He's sulking.
-[chuckles]

15:18.709 --> 15:20.169
This place looks nice.

15:25.550 --> 15:26.759
Wow.

15:27.468 --> 15:30.179
It's shattered and cracked.

15:31.597 --> 15:34.183
And there seem to be
some pieces missing. Hmm?

15:35.768 --> 15:36.769
Will it be too hard?

15:41.399 --> 15:42.400
[sighs dejectedly]

15:43.234 --> 15:45.027
I can make it work.

15:45.111 --> 15:47.029
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]
-[exclaims]

15:47.113 --> 15:48.406
It may take some time,

15:48.489 --> 15:51.826
but as long as we don't give up,
it can be fixed somehow.

15:51.909 --> 15:53.161
[sighs in relief]

15:53.244 --> 15:55.204
[Chan's grandma]
It would be different from the original,

15:55.288 --> 15:57.582
but let's think of it
as making it stronger.

15:57.665 --> 15:59.542
Thank you so much.

15:59.625 --> 16:01.502
Here's your coffee.

16:01.586 --> 16:03.004
[Chan's grandma chuckles]

16:03.087 --> 16:06.048
My grandson must be troubling you a lot.

16:06.757 --> 16:09.552
If he does anything to irritate you,

16:09.635 --> 16:13.055
you can just smack him on the back
and kick him out.

16:13.139 --> 16:14.515
Really?

16:14.599 --> 16:18.352
He's been nagging me so much lately
that I've been thinking about it.

16:19.061 --> 16:21.314
I will keep that in mind.

16:21.397 --> 16:22.481
[all laugh]

16:22.565 --> 16:24.692
-Stop it.
-[Chan clears throat]

16:24.775 --> 16:28.404
You must be curious about the house.
You can take a look after you're done.

16:28.487 --> 16:31.741
No, it's your private space. I shouldn't…

16:31.824 --> 16:34.076
It's fine. It's also Chan's house.

16:34.160 --> 16:35.369
Give her a tour later.

16:36.621 --> 16:41.459
Seeing you stay with someone so nice
makes me feel at ease.

16:42.084 --> 16:43.419
[Chan's grandma chuckles]

16:43.502 --> 16:45.421
Be good to him, all right?

16:45.504 --> 16:46.547
I will.

16:47.215 --> 16:48.216
[♪ music fades]

16:48.299 --> 16:50.927
Wow. [chuckling]

16:51.636 --> 16:52.720
[gasps]

16:58.643 --> 17:02.271
So how about letting time with your dad
start moving again?

17:08.361 --> 17:09.362
Chan.

17:11.781 --> 17:13.324
[stutters] It's nothing. Never mind.

17:14.075 --> 17:16.911
[in singsong] It was nothing. [chuckles]

17:20.289 --> 17:22.333
-When will you visit again?
-[both chuckle]

17:23.209 --> 17:25.253
That little brat isn't even seeing me off.

17:25.336 --> 17:26.420
I should give him a smack.

17:26.504 --> 17:27.713
[Chan] Grandma.

17:28.589 --> 17:30.132
Can you drop me off on the way?

17:31.634 --> 17:32.718
Where?

17:33.302 --> 17:34.303
Daejeon.

17:34.387 --> 17:36.639
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

17:37.807 --> 17:39.850
I don't know what I'll do there,

17:40.601 --> 17:42.979
but I think
I should at least give this back to him.

17:44.939 --> 17:45.940
[Chan] Mm.

17:47.733 --> 17:48.943
[chuckling]

17:52.863 --> 17:54.240
[Chan's grandma exclaims softly]

17:54.323 --> 17:55.324
[♪ music fades]

17:57.535 --> 17:59.120
[Hadam's friend]
I saw Yougyum this weekend.

17:59.203 --> 18:01.330
He was going to karaoke with his friends.

18:05.376 --> 18:07.086
[Hadam] Are you having
a lot of fun these days?

18:07.587 --> 18:09.380
Did you have fun at karaoke?

18:10.923 --> 18:12.675
What? I…

18:12.758 --> 18:14.760
[♪ amusing music playing]

18:17.597 --> 18:19.599
Yeah, I had fun.

18:20.266 --> 18:22.143
You seemed to be having fun, too.

18:22.977 --> 18:25.563
You gave Seokhyeon
a drink with a heart on it.

18:26.272 --> 18:27.273
What?

18:27.356 --> 18:28.482
[sighs]

18:28.566 --> 18:29.567
So you saw it.

18:29.984 --> 18:31.360
Yeah, I'm happy these days.

18:31.444 --> 18:33.404
I'm really glad to hear that.

18:33.487 --> 18:35.990
Yeah, so let's both live happy lives.

18:41.746 --> 18:42.747
[♪ music fades]

18:42.830 --> 18:45.583
CHEMICAL AND BIOLOGICAL ENGINEERING
PROFESSOR SUNWOO SEOK

18:56.010 --> 18:57.219
[sighs]

19:03.059 --> 19:04.101
May I help you?

19:05.519 --> 19:08.022
Oh. I'm here to see Professor Sunwoo.

19:08.105 --> 19:09.440
[assistant] Ah.

19:09.523 --> 19:11.108
He's gone to the president's office.

19:11.192 --> 19:13.694
-May I ask what you're here for?
-[hesitates]

19:16.113 --> 19:17.448
We're family.

19:18.407 --> 19:20.701
-If he's not here--
-He'll probably be back soon.

19:21.118 --> 19:22.328
Why don't you wait inside?

19:22.620 --> 19:24.038
Ah…

19:24.121 --> 19:25.748
[sighs softly]

19:25.831 --> 19:27.833
[♪ pensive music playing]

19:43.766 --> 19:45.476
-[knocks on door]
-[door opens]

19:45.559 --> 19:47.478
He's taking a while.

19:47.561 --> 19:48.729
Should I try calling him?

19:50.189 --> 19:52.233
No, I'll just go.

19:52.900 --> 19:56.570
[hesitates] Would it be okay
to leave this here?

19:57.113 --> 19:58.239
Sure, go ahead.

20:00.449 --> 20:01.450
[♪ music fades]

20:03.953 --> 20:04.954
[door closes]

20:08.708 --> 20:11.585
KOREA SCIENCE UNIVERSITY

20:14.338 --> 20:16.090
Let me keep this, Dad.

20:16.173 --> 20:17.842
-[young Chan gasps]
-[door slams]

20:17.925 --> 20:20.428
[♪ sentimental music playing]

20:44.452 --> 20:46.120
How long are you going to keep doing this?

20:46.203 --> 20:48.873
What more do I have to do
to make you stop?

21:17.443 --> 21:18.778
[sighs heavily]

21:21.197 --> 21:22.198
[sniffles]

21:32.792 --> 21:33.793
[♪ music fades]

21:33.876 --> 21:35.461
Excuse me, you said you're family.

21:36.045 --> 21:39.882
Are you his son who's working
as an animator in the US?

21:40.382 --> 21:41.383
You are, right?

21:41.967 --> 21:44.011
I heard a lot about you
from Professor Sunwoo.

21:44.512 --> 21:46.972
He always rushes to see
any movies that get released.

21:47.056 --> 21:49.475
He even buys tickets for his students.

21:52.728 --> 21:55.147
[♪ slow instrumental music
playing on speakers]

21:58.692 --> 21:59.944
[Haran clears throat]

22:00.027 --> 22:01.153
[Haran clears throat loudly]

22:05.574 --> 22:06.992
Can I ask you something, sir?

22:07.076 --> 22:09.787
I heard there's a famous bakery nearby.

22:10.287 --> 22:11.497
Do you know where it is?

22:13.082 --> 22:14.708
-Excuse me?
-[chuckles softly]

22:14.792 --> 22:16.335
I came here to buy bread.

22:16.418 --> 22:19.088
I heard there's
a really famous bakery here.

22:21.257 --> 22:23.676
[sighs] You're such a bad liar.

22:24.301 --> 22:26.846
Were you worried
something would've happened again?

22:26.929 --> 22:28.264
Well…

22:28.347 --> 22:30.558
I also came to check
Daejeon's fashion trends.

22:30.641 --> 22:31.642
[gasps] Wow.

22:31.725 --> 22:33.978
Everyone's so fashionable here.

22:36.230 --> 22:39.650
And I thought that if anything happened,

22:39.733 --> 22:41.527
I could give you a hug.

22:41.610 --> 22:43.946
[inhales sharply] Look at you.

22:44.864 --> 22:48.117
When going to Gyeongju,
at the airport, and now Daejeon…

22:48.868 --> 22:51.245
You keep surprising me like this.

22:51.954 --> 22:53.914
You'll make me get my hopes up.

22:55.708 --> 22:58.752
I'll keep thinking you'll appear anywhere.

23:01.714 --> 23:02.715
Fine.

23:03.299 --> 23:06.594
I'll appear anywhere you are,
so you can get your hopes up.

23:09.722 --> 23:10.723
[man] Seonu Chan!

23:34.038 --> 23:37.166
[assistant] I'm so glad you've recovered.

23:38.000 --> 23:41.045
Professor Sunwoo gave up on his research
just before presenting it

23:41.128 --> 23:45.215
to go take care of you in America
when you were badly injured.

23:45.299 --> 23:46.717
[doctor in English]
We've done everything we can.

23:46.800 --> 23:49.011
Now we just have to hope
that he'll pull through.

23:49.094 --> 23:50.721
The truth is, you should be aware

23:50.804 --> 23:52.431
it's not very likely that he'll wake up.

23:52.514 --> 23:54.767
[♪ emotional music playing]

24:08.948 --> 24:10.950
[♪ emotional music continuing]

24:16.664 --> 24:17.665
[in Korean] Thanks…

24:18.540 --> 24:19.750
for the watch.

24:20.376 --> 24:21.460
[sighs]

24:24.463 --> 24:27.967
[exhales nervously]
Maybe you should return your degree.

24:29.510 --> 24:32.930
A famous engineering professor
can't even fix a broken watch?

24:34.223 --> 24:36.725
It's working well now.

24:38.352 --> 24:39.436
Thank you…

24:40.521 --> 24:41.563
for fixing it.

24:45.859 --> 24:47.069
If you're grateful,

24:49.154 --> 24:51.740
you can pay me back later.

25:05.671 --> 25:07.673
[♪ music continues]

25:50.883 --> 25:51.884
[♪ music ends]

25:51.967 --> 25:53.886
Grandma called.

25:54.344 --> 25:55.971
She thanked me and said I did well.

25:56.055 --> 25:57.056
[Haran] Really?

25:57.765 --> 25:58.807
That's great.

25:59.349 --> 26:02.269
I'm so glad you gave it back to him.

26:02.352 --> 26:05.481
That watch must be
dozens of times more precious now.

26:06.023 --> 26:08.692
It could have ended
with him being sad about losing it,

26:08.776 --> 26:12.571
but now, it's the watch that his son
fixed and returned to him.

26:23.665 --> 26:26.085
Can I see you for a moment again?

26:26.585 --> 26:28.796
[♪ relaxing music playing on speakers]

26:29.838 --> 26:30.839
Huh?

26:33.550 --> 26:34.843
How did you…

26:34.927 --> 26:38.097
Remember when we went to that restaurant?

26:38.889 --> 26:41.183
When I was in bad shape because of my ear.

26:41.683 --> 26:42.768
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[groans]

26:42.851 --> 26:43.894
[server yelps]

26:43.977 --> 26:46.188
It's noisy in there.
I'll go bring our stuff.

26:46.647 --> 26:49.817
It must have gotten mixed up
in my stuff back then.

26:50.776 --> 26:53.070
I found it
when I unpacked my luggage here.

26:53.946 --> 26:54.947
Ah…

26:58.408 --> 27:00.702
I don't need it anymore, though.

27:06.458 --> 27:08.043
I'm already using a different one.

27:08.502 --> 27:10.712
Plus, I have dozens of pens now.

27:10.796 --> 27:13.549
Someone gave me a whole bunch
as a gift. [chuckles softly]

27:16.218 --> 27:18.053
That's why I'm giving it back now.

27:18.137 --> 27:19.179
I…

27:20.222 --> 27:22.266
was worried that I'd remind you

27:23.183 --> 27:25.477
of the memories back then.

27:26.311 --> 27:28.438
But I thought you wouldn't be wavered now.

27:29.898 --> 27:33.694
Just think of it as a pen
that's the most effective and use it.

27:35.237 --> 27:39.449
I know how important it is
to have a tool that fits you just right

27:39.533 --> 27:41.368
since I'm an animator.

27:42.536 --> 27:45.163
I can just get used to this pen.

27:48.792 --> 27:50.502
Let me borrow this for a second.

27:55.507 --> 27:57.467
[♪ pleasant song playing]

27:57.551 --> 27:59.553
[pen scraping]

28:05.392 --> 28:07.811
[breathes deeply]

28:09.646 --> 28:11.732
Just consider this pen

28:12.441 --> 28:15.444
a pen that I found for you,
not a pen that you got as a gift

28:17.195 --> 28:20.198
or a pen that made you sad
when you lost it.

28:21.742 --> 28:25.162
And… here's a lucky charm.

28:25.245 --> 28:28.248
You know you'll get lucky
once you see an iridescent cloud.

28:28.957 --> 28:30.667
You can see one every day now,

28:31.251 --> 28:34.129
so you'll be lucky every day.
[chuckles softly]

28:39.509 --> 28:42.220
-[sighs]
-[inhales sharply, grunts]

28:42.304 --> 28:43.430
Just use it.

28:46.058 --> 28:49.227
I sincerely want you to use it again.

28:53.774 --> 28:54.775
All right.

28:56.068 --> 28:57.361
I will.

29:00.030 --> 29:01.907
It's the pen you found for me now.

29:17.214 --> 29:18.715
[cell phone vibrating]

29:20.300 --> 29:21.510
Hello?

29:24.429 --> 29:25.430
[exclaims] Really?

29:26.848 --> 29:28.767
[exclaims softly] All right.

29:28.850 --> 29:30.727
Thank you. Okay.

29:31.853 --> 29:32.854
[sighs]

29:34.231 --> 29:35.565
No way.

29:36.483 --> 29:38.568
-This is crazy.
-What is it?

29:38.652 --> 29:40.320
Something good really happened.

29:40.988 --> 29:42.572
I'm receiving an award.

29:42.656 --> 29:44.741
The Best Designer Award
at the Fashion Awards.

29:45.367 --> 29:47.327
See? I told you that you'd be lucky.

29:47.411 --> 29:49.621
-[chuckles softly]
-Congratulations.

29:51.331 --> 29:52.332
[♪ song fades]

30:04.594 --> 30:05.971
[Manjae] Genius.

30:07.472 --> 30:08.849
Are you here?

30:08.932 --> 30:09.933
Huh?

30:11.101 --> 30:12.102
Hey, Genius.

30:13.603 --> 30:14.604
[Genius barks]

30:15.313 --> 30:16.523
Is there something there?

30:18.650 --> 30:20.068
[Manjae exclaims] What…

30:20.902 --> 30:21.903
Nabong!

30:21.987 --> 30:23.196
[♪ somber music playing]

30:23.280 --> 30:25.323
What are you doing here at this hour?

30:25.407 --> 30:26.491
Hey, Manjae.

30:26.992 --> 30:30.579
I wanted to get a cup of coffee
after I finished work,

30:30.662 --> 30:32.330
but I didn't realize it was so late.

30:34.041 --> 30:37.169
The snow was beautiful,
so I was watching it for a bit.

30:37.252 --> 30:38.879
-[♪ music fades]
-It's so late…

30:38.962 --> 30:40.881
And you're dressed so lightly.

30:41.339 --> 30:42.340
It's cold.

30:42.424 --> 30:43.675
Come on, let's go inside.

30:45.927 --> 30:47.262
Get yourself warmed up.

30:49.848 --> 30:52.142
What on earth is going on?

30:52.225 --> 30:55.145
I was so absorbed in work,
I didn't notice the time.

30:55.771 --> 30:57.939
You know how focused I can get.

31:02.402 --> 31:03.820
Are you sure nothing's wrong?

31:05.781 --> 31:07.240
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

31:07.324 --> 31:08.700
Is everything really okay?

31:08.784 --> 31:10.786
Is this some trending challenge?

31:11.286 --> 31:13.789
Why is everyone asking me that? [chuckles]

31:14.956 --> 31:18.168
Did I neglect my skincare
because I was too busy?

31:27.594 --> 31:30.055
Have some warm tea.

31:45.821 --> 31:47.155
[sighs]

31:48.323 --> 31:49.574
[Manjae] What on earth

31:50.367 --> 31:52.619
is going on with you?

31:57.707 --> 31:58.708
[♪ music ends]

31:58.792 --> 32:00.794
[♪ upbeat music playing on speakers]

32:07.259 --> 32:09.386
LAUNDRY DETERGENT
LAVENDER

32:11.471 --> 32:13.265
[woman] Aren't you my Hadam?

32:13.348 --> 32:15.392
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

32:16.935 --> 32:18.103
It's me.

32:19.354 --> 32:21.022
Mom.

32:22.315 --> 32:23.650
Mom?

32:24.818 --> 32:26.027
-Oh, my goodness!
-[♪ music fades]

32:26.111 --> 32:28.238
I finally got to meet you.

32:28.321 --> 32:30.031
I wanted to see you so much.

32:30.115 --> 32:32.826
It's me, Yougyum's mom.

32:32.909 --> 32:34.578
What? Ah…

32:35.704 --> 32:36.705
Ah!

32:37.539 --> 32:38.707
Hello.

32:38.790 --> 32:40.917
[Yougyum's mom]
Goodness, it's so nice to meet you.

32:41.001 --> 32:42.752
I recognized you right away.

32:42.836 --> 32:45.839
Our house is plastered with photos of you.

32:45.922 --> 32:48.884
-[chuckles awkwardly]
-I feel like I'm meeting a celebrity.

32:48.967 --> 32:52.888
If it's all right, could I give you a hug?

32:57.309 --> 33:00.187
[chuckling] My dear Hadam.

33:00.270 --> 33:03.481
It's so nice to see you.

33:03.565 --> 33:05.567
[♪ emotional music playing]

33:07.110 --> 33:08.820
[breathing shakily]

33:09.654 --> 33:11.406
[whimpering]

33:11.489 --> 33:13.909
[Yougyum's mom] What's wrong? What is it?

33:14.743 --> 33:19.873
[Hyewon] ♪ Sleep well, dear Hadam ♪

33:19.956 --> 33:24.211
♪ Sleep in Mommy's arms ♪

33:24.294 --> 33:29.299
♪ Sleep well, dear Hadam ♪

33:29.799 --> 33:34.095
♪ Sleep tight ♪

33:34.179 --> 33:35.347
I found…

33:39.517 --> 33:40.810
Mom's smell.

33:42.145 --> 33:43.313
[Hadam crying]

33:47.943 --> 33:49.277
-[stomach rumbles]
-[gasps]

33:53.114 --> 33:55.283
[laughing]

33:55.784 --> 33:58.078
Come on. I'll make you a meal.

33:59.246 --> 34:01.748
[laughing] Let's go.

34:02.540 --> 34:04.000
[man in English] Excuse me.

34:04.084 --> 34:05.627
Where is the grocery store?

34:05.710 --> 34:06.920
-[steam hissing]
-[♪ music fades]

34:07.003 --> 34:08.380
[chuckles] Excuse me.

34:08.463 --> 34:10.006
Where is the grocery store?

34:10.090 --> 34:12.759
-[Yougyum's mom in Korean] Honey.
-Come on in.

34:12.842 --> 34:13.843
[chuckling]

34:16.054 --> 34:17.305
Hello.

34:17.931 --> 34:19.182
Look who it is!

34:19.266 --> 34:20.850
Isn't she our superstar?

34:20.934 --> 34:22.727
-Our dear Hadam.
-Ah…

34:22.811 --> 34:24.437
We told Yougyum to bring you,

34:24.521 --> 34:26.648
but he said
we shouldn't bother your studies

34:26.731 --> 34:29.317
and kept you hidden all along.

34:29.401 --> 34:31.236
I ran into her by chance
at the supermarket.

34:31.319 --> 34:32.988
Welcome.

34:33.071 --> 34:34.155
Did you eat?

34:34.239 --> 34:35.407
Join us for a meal.

34:35.490 --> 34:36.616
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

34:36.700 --> 34:40.203
Gosh. I told you to bring me
when you're buying heavy stuff.

34:40.287 --> 34:42.497
I'll bring these upstairs. [chuckles]

34:42.580 --> 34:43.832
-[thuds]
-[groans] Gosh!

34:43.915 --> 34:45.250
My goodness.

34:45.834 --> 34:47.836
[Yougyum's mom and Hadam chuckle]

34:49.212 --> 34:52.424
[Hadam exclaims] I can't believe him.

34:57.345 --> 34:59.556
LET'S BE SOMEONE HADAM WILL BE PROUD OF!

35:00.432 --> 35:02.809
[Yougyum's mom] I wondered why
he only got perfect scores in English.

35:03.268 --> 35:05.478
I heard you told him in your first year.

35:05.562 --> 35:07.147
The Major League?

35:07.230 --> 35:08.773
If that's your goal,

35:08.857 --> 35:11.735
shouldn't you at least
study English in advance?

35:11.818 --> 35:14.362
[in English] I want to be better
than I was yesterday.

35:14.696 --> 35:15.697
"Challenge."

35:16.031 --> 35:17.032
[in Korean] Challenge.

35:17.115 --> 35:20.160
[Yougyum's mom] Since then,
his father has been studying English, too.

35:20.243 --> 35:22.245
He said he wants to help Yougyum.

35:22.329 --> 35:24.998
This is how much influence
you have over our family.

35:25.081 --> 35:26.082
[chuckles shyly]

35:26.166 --> 35:27.417
[♪ music fades]

35:27.500 --> 35:29.002
He's unbelievable.

35:29.085 --> 35:31.671
[Yougyum's dad]
Honey, should I braise the fish?

35:31.755 --> 35:32.922
Hang on.

35:33.006 --> 35:34.716
-Sorry. Take a look around.
-Okay.

35:39.346 --> 35:43.016
[Yougyum's mom]
But how did you end up dating Yougyum?

35:43.099 --> 35:46.061
He said he had a crush on you
since elementary school.

35:46.144 --> 35:48.605
[Hadam] Thinking back,

35:49.105 --> 35:51.566
he was the only one who understood me.

35:51.650 --> 35:53.485
[♪ sentimental music playing]

35:53.568 --> 35:55.862
[kid 1] Why aren't your parents
here for the field day?

35:55.945 --> 35:59.449
[kid 2] Hey, she's the poor kid
whose parents both died.

35:59.532 --> 36:01.034
[kid 1] Really? That's so pitiful.

36:01.117 --> 36:05.080
Hey, having your parents
pass away isn't pitiful.

36:05.163 --> 36:06.373
It's just sad.

36:07.749 --> 36:09.084
[Hadam groans]

36:10.085 --> 36:12.837
I solved this when I stayed up
studying last night.

36:12.921 --> 36:14.214
Hadam.

36:14.964 --> 36:18.218
In baseball, throwing pull power
every time will strain your body.

36:18.301 --> 36:20.512
You need a breather to grow stronger.

36:20.595 --> 36:22.138
A breather?

36:23.473 --> 36:24.474
That's why…

36:27.352 --> 36:28.478
you need a breather now.

36:30.271 --> 36:32.524
All right. Pitcher Cha Yougyum
is ready to throw.

36:35.068 --> 36:36.069
-[Yougyum groans]
-[sighs]

36:37.320 --> 36:38.321
[both exclaim excitedly]

36:38.405 --> 36:39.447
I hit it!

36:39.531 --> 36:40.907
Run, Hadam!

36:42.242 --> 36:43.535
Go!

36:43.618 --> 36:45.662
[♪ pleasant music playing]

36:48.873 --> 36:49.958
Right.

36:53.545 --> 36:56.965
Yougyum always understood me.

36:58.133 --> 37:00.218
-[♪ music ends]
-[cell phone buzzes]

37:04.597 --> 37:07.350
[Manjae] Nabong, guess what I found?

37:08.601 --> 37:09.602
[gasps softly]

37:09.686 --> 37:11.521
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

37:16.651 --> 37:19.529
Manjae, where did you get that photo?

37:19.612 --> 37:20.655
Oh. [chuckles]

37:20.739 --> 37:22.657
I was organizing my vinyl collection,

37:22.741 --> 37:25.618
-and it just fell out.
-[Nana gasps on phone]

37:25.702 --> 37:28.788
I can't believe it.
That was such a long time ago.

37:28.872 --> 37:30.457
I wonder if that tree is still there.

37:31.416 --> 37:36.171
Remember the tteokbokki place
we used to go to in the market?

37:36.588 --> 37:37.672
What was it called?

37:37.756 --> 37:39.883
-Ah! Fat Tteokbokki.
-Fat Tteokbokki.

37:39.966 --> 37:41.760
-[Manjae] Right?
-[laughs]

37:41.843 --> 37:43.261
[laughs]

37:43.344 --> 37:46.431
Ah… I'm craving
that super sweet tteokbokki.

37:47.182 --> 37:50.185
Do you want to go
have tteokbokki this evening?

37:51.853 --> 37:53.354
[hesitates] No…

37:53.438 --> 37:55.815
You shouldn't ditch work, right?

37:55.899 --> 37:57.442
Come on.

37:57.525 --> 38:00.779
Nabong, have you forgotten
that I'm the owner?

38:01.821 --> 38:03.615
I can totally ditch work.

38:03.698 --> 38:04.699
[♪ music fades]

38:05.575 --> 38:06.618
Well, well.

38:06.701 --> 38:09.204
I caught you. Are you ditching work?

38:09.287 --> 38:10.955
No, I'm receiving an award.

38:11.039 --> 38:13.291
Oh, right. The Fashion Awards is today.

38:13.374 --> 38:15.168
-Congratulations.
-[chuckles softly]

38:15.251 --> 38:16.544
See you.

38:18.129 --> 38:20.131
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

38:20.215 --> 38:21.925
[footsteps echoing]

38:24.719 --> 38:26.179
[Raemee exclaims] Love.

38:26.262 --> 38:29.098
That means you like him too.

38:29.182 --> 38:30.975
[Hayeong] No way.

38:31.059 --> 38:32.060
Was he right?

38:32.143 --> 38:35.355
Why does he look so cool
when he's just walking?

38:35.438 --> 38:36.689
[suit rustle echoes]

38:40.568 --> 38:42.237
Why am I blushing?

38:42.320 --> 38:43.863
And why am I sweating?

38:51.079 --> 38:53.331
Are you free this evening?

38:53.414 --> 38:55.917
[Hayeong] This evening?
Not morning or afternoon?

38:56.543 --> 38:58.962
Is he asking me out?

38:59.045 --> 39:00.922
[gasps inwardly] On a date?

39:01.005 --> 39:03.091
I got a reply that the factory

39:03.174 --> 39:05.635
couldn't get any of the bio silk
you talked about.

39:05.718 --> 39:06.928
I did more research

39:07.011 --> 39:10.598
and got in touch with an industry
tech reporter who wrote about it.

39:10.682 --> 39:12.475
We're meeting this evening.

39:12.559 --> 39:14.811
We may find a way to do it.

39:14.894 --> 39:18.147
[Hayeong] Mr. Yeon's cheeks
seem a little red, too.

39:18.648 --> 39:20.859
Huh? And he's sweating.

39:20.942 --> 39:22.193
Was Raemee really right?

39:22.277 --> 39:25.238
Then we really like each other?

39:25.822 --> 39:27.365
[clinking]

39:28.283 --> 39:30.994
Great job with the meeting.

39:34.706 --> 39:36.124
How about some wine?

39:36.207 --> 39:37.542
Just you and me,

39:38.126 --> 39:39.168
alone.

39:40.003 --> 39:42.046
Sure. I'd like that.

39:42.630 --> 39:44.257
Pardon? Uh…

39:44.883 --> 39:47.093
Are you saying you'll come?

39:47.844 --> 39:48.845
[♪ music fades]

39:48.928 --> 39:50.179
Ah.

39:50.263 --> 39:52.223
Yes, I'm free.

39:52.307 --> 39:54.225
I'll drive, then.

39:54.309 --> 39:56.519
I'll see you at the parking lot
at 7:00 p.m.

40:01.900 --> 40:02.901
[sighs]

40:03.693 --> 40:05.987
Why are we meeting at 7:00 p.m.?

40:07.655 --> 40:09.073
Right.

40:09.157 --> 40:10.199
The new material.

40:11.534 --> 40:12.535
The meeting.

40:12.619 --> 40:13.953
GYUM'S LAUNDRY

40:14.037 --> 40:15.580
[Yougyum] I'm home.

40:18.666 --> 40:19.876
Mom.

40:19.959 --> 40:22.211
Mom, I must have lost my mind.

40:22.295 --> 40:25.757
I miss Hadam so much,
I must be hallucinating.

40:27.467 --> 40:29.385
But… [breathing shakily]

40:29.469 --> 40:32.263
it's still so nice to see her.

40:32.347 --> 40:34.349
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

40:36.184 --> 40:37.185
[Yougyum sniffles]

40:37.894 --> 40:39.062
You idiot.

40:39.979 --> 40:41.230
It's really me.

40:41.856 --> 40:43.232
Wow.

40:43.316 --> 40:44.484
She's even talking now.

40:45.234 --> 40:48.863
I must have gone crazy
from missing her so much.

40:48.947 --> 40:50.365
You idiot.

40:51.783 --> 40:53.451
It really is me.

40:54.953 --> 40:58.122
[stuttering] Is it really you?

40:58.206 --> 41:00.124
You're really Hadam?

41:00.208 --> 41:02.710
I didn't give Seokhyeon my number.

41:02.794 --> 41:06.589
Someone left a drink at my seat
with a heart post-it,

41:06.673 --> 41:09.008
and I rushed out thinking it was from you.

41:09.467 --> 41:12.011
When I heard it was from Seokhyeon,
I gave it back to him.

41:16.224 --> 41:17.225
Really?

41:17.850 --> 41:19.143
I'm sorry I misunderstood.

41:19.727 --> 41:21.604
I wasn't having fun at karaoke either.

41:21.688 --> 41:23.940
My friends took me there to comfort me,

41:24.524 --> 41:26.609
but I just kept crying
at the thought of you.

41:26.693 --> 41:28.778
I'm sorry I misunderstood you, too.

41:29.862 --> 41:32.490
But why are you wearing glasses?

41:32.991 --> 41:34.367
Has your eyesight gotten bad?

41:34.909 --> 41:35.910
No,

41:37.286 --> 41:38.579
I don't need them now.

41:38.663 --> 41:41.457
And you? Why were you
at the nurse's office? Were you sick?

41:43.084 --> 41:44.085
[breathing shakily]

41:44.168 --> 41:45.920
I just got a small cut on my hand,

41:46.671 --> 41:48.297
-but I'm all better now.
-[sniffling]

41:54.637 --> 41:56.931
[both crying]

41:57.015 --> 41:58.599
I'm sorry, Hadam.

41:58.683 --> 42:00.977
[crying] I'm more sorry.

42:01.060 --> 42:02.812
[Yougyum] I missed you so much.

42:02.895 --> 42:05.648
[Hadam] I missed you even more.

42:05.732 --> 42:08.735
-[♪ grandiose music playing on speakers]
-[announcer] The Best Designer Award.

42:08.818 --> 42:11.195
-Nana Atelier, Song Haran.
-[applause]

42:11.279 --> 42:13.156
There are two winners this year.

42:13.239 --> 42:15.616
-Onne Apparel, Kang Eunchan.
-[cameras clicking]

42:15.700 --> 42:16.993
[applause]

42:26.544 --> 42:27.545
[♪ music fades]

42:27.628 --> 42:28.629
[Eunchan] Haran.

42:29.088 --> 42:31.632
I have to go to the factory.
There's a fabric issue.

42:31.716 --> 42:34.218
I booked a table at Haeon,
the restaurant nearby.

42:35.470 --> 42:36.512
Take this and go there.

42:36.596 --> 42:40.266
I said I'd buy dinner for my brother,
but I can't let him eat alone.

42:40.349 --> 42:42.769
Sorry, but just have dinner
with him, okay?

42:44.145 --> 42:46.773
-♪ Happy birthday to you ♪
-[clapping]

42:46.856 --> 42:48.858
-[♪ pleasant music playing]
-♪ Happy birthday… ♪

42:48.941 --> 42:50.318
-[yawns]
-[chuckles]

42:50.985 --> 42:54.280
I'm sorry. I haven't slept
for the past three days.

42:54.363 --> 42:56.282
Sorry. Right.

42:56.365 --> 42:57.909
♪ Happy birthday, dear… ♪

42:57.992 --> 42:59.410
Kang Hyeokchan.

42:59.494 --> 43:01.370
♪ Kang Hyeokchan ♪

43:01.454 --> 43:03.247
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

43:03.331 --> 43:04.373
[cheers]

43:08.169 --> 43:10.797
A Mr. Kang from our house
asked me to give it to you.

43:11.255 --> 43:12.799
-What?
-Good luck.

43:13.466 --> 43:14.842
VITAMINS FOR ENERGY
A CUSHION FOR A NAP

43:14.926 --> 43:16.427
CHOCOLATE AFTER LUNCH
CHAMOMILE AFTER WORK

43:16.511 --> 43:17.553
WITH THESE, YOU CAN SLEEP BETTER

43:19.180 --> 43:20.181
[chuckles softly]

43:24.477 --> 43:25.937
[kisses, chuckles]

43:26.020 --> 43:27.230
-I love you.
-Hmm?

43:28.231 --> 43:29.315
That's so sudden.

43:30.441 --> 43:32.110
-[scoffs]
-[cell phone vibrating]

43:33.486 --> 43:34.737
[sighs wearily]

43:35.321 --> 43:36.322
It's work.

43:37.406 --> 43:39.200
Good luck with the embassy interview.

43:42.578 --> 43:43.621
Hello?

43:43.955 --> 43:47.125
[sighs] I can't believe I have to work
when you're leaving.

43:47.208 --> 43:48.543
I'm so sorry, Chan.

43:49.252 --> 43:50.503
It's fine.

43:50.586 --> 43:52.839
I told you I won't get upset
about you being busy.

43:52.922 --> 43:55.007
I'll be back during vacation. I love you.

43:55.091 --> 43:56.342
I'm so sorry.

43:56.425 --> 43:58.094
Leave me a message when you arrive.

43:58.386 --> 43:59.387
[cell phone pings]

43:59.470 --> 44:02.932
[Hyeokchan] I can't go back to Korea
because of my lab schedule.

44:03.015 --> 44:05.935
And my phone's broken,
so I won't be able to text for a while.

44:06.602 --> 44:08.688
Leave me a message
if there's anything urgent.

44:08.771 --> 44:10.439
[Hayeong] I knew it.

44:10.898 --> 44:12.817
Are you sure he just doesn't want to come?

44:13.317 --> 44:15.736
-What?
-Well, I haven't seen it myself,

44:15.820 --> 44:18.447
but he was so nice to you
when he was in Seoul.

44:18.531 --> 44:21.242
But you were always busy
and didn't keep in touch often.

44:21.325 --> 44:22.952
You didn't even show much affection.

44:23.035 --> 44:24.662
You'll get dumped at this rate.

44:24.745 --> 44:27.415
[sighs] You're right.
I guess I deserve it.

44:28.416 --> 44:29.625
That's too bad.

44:29.709 --> 44:31.794
What's that reaction?

44:31.878 --> 44:33.796
Do you even like Hyeokchan?

44:33.880 --> 44:36.424
Of course I do. He's my boyfriend.

44:36.507 --> 44:38.217
[Hayeong] No, not like that.

44:38.801 --> 44:40.052
Do you love him?

44:40.678 --> 44:41.679
[Haran] Mmm?

44:42.221 --> 44:43.556
[Eunchan] Did Chan send that?

44:43.639 --> 44:45.892
He sent a drawing pen
for his designer girlfriend?

44:46.976 --> 44:49.812
Wow. And even with your name
engraved on it?

44:51.939 --> 44:54.859
[Haran] But how did you come up
with the idea of sending me a pen?

44:54.942 --> 44:56.277
[♪ sentimental music playing]

44:56.360 --> 44:58.738
I KEPT THINKING ABOUT HOW YOU SAID
YOU FELT LIKE YOU WERE TRAPPED

44:58.821 --> 45:00.781
I GUESS I WANTED THAT PEN
TO BE THAT "IF" FOR YOU

45:00.865 --> 45:01.991
[sighs]

45:02.491 --> 45:05.161
Chan understands me so well…

45:05.828 --> 45:06.829
SORRY, I WAS RAMBLING

45:07.788 --> 45:11.417
I miss you, Hyeokchan.

45:12.752 --> 45:15.504
Ta-da! I'm at the airport!

45:15.630 --> 45:17.715
I wanted to tell you something in person.

45:18.090 --> 45:20.218
Chan. I love you.

45:21.719 --> 45:23.804
I love you, Chan. [chuckles]

45:23.888 --> 45:25.264
[Eunchan] Haran, what do I do?

45:25.348 --> 45:26.349
Chan…

45:26.849 --> 45:29.477
-Hyeokchan is dead.
-[siren blaring]

45:36.567 --> 45:38.694
-[♪ music fades]
-[applause]

45:42.323 --> 45:44.116
[Eunchan] I moved to Onne Apparel.

45:45.326 --> 45:48.788
It's awkward giving you my business card.

45:52.208 --> 45:54.126
Have you been well?

45:56.587 --> 45:57.755
It's already been…

45:58.881 --> 45:59.882
seven years.

46:01.217 --> 46:03.970
I always wondered how you were doing,

46:04.512 --> 46:06.180
but I felt too guilty to contact you.

46:06.931 --> 46:09.725
Why would you feel guilty?

46:18.067 --> 46:19.944
-What is it?
-Oh…

46:21.320 --> 46:24.532
Were you getting checkups here?

46:24.615 --> 46:25.616
Huh?

46:26.534 --> 46:28.286
Ahh.

46:28.369 --> 46:31.664
I was at a different ER
when I collapsed last time.

46:31.747 --> 46:33.040
[chuckles]

46:33.124 --> 46:35.626
I got a referral, so I come here.

46:35.710 --> 46:36.877
It's closer.

46:36.961 --> 46:38.296
-What is it?
-Ah…

46:39.005 --> 46:42.550
I got treated here before.
[chuckles softly]

46:43.509 --> 46:46.429
I'll go ask where we can get the results.

46:52.560 --> 46:54.103
We have to go to the annex.

46:54.729 --> 46:55.813
Really?

46:56.772 --> 46:59.025
But why are you dressed up today?

47:00.192 --> 47:01.402
[Manjae] Hmm?

47:01.485 --> 47:04.780
I have to be dressed up
to go somewhere later.

47:05.364 --> 47:07.283
-[inhales sharply] Mmm…
-[Manjae chuckles]

47:07.366 --> 47:08.534
[Chan] Where are you going?

47:14.040 --> 47:15.041
[automation] The door is closing.

47:15.124 --> 47:17.460
[automation in English]
The door is closing.

47:18.627 --> 47:20.880
[metallic clinking]

47:24.050 --> 47:26.469
[metallic clinking]

47:26.802 --> 47:28.054
[elevator dings]

47:31.766 --> 47:33.976
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

47:34.060 --> 47:36.854
[in Korean] Huh? Hey, roomie!

47:37.438 --> 47:38.689
[pants]

47:41.317 --> 47:42.943
[metallic clinking echoes]

47:44.028 --> 47:46.197
[metallic clinking]

47:52.828 --> 47:55.081
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[panting]

47:57.833 --> 47:58.834
Mr. Park.

48:00.169 --> 48:02.838
Sorry, I'll head over there.

48:05.383 --> 48:06.384
Okay.

48:12.681 --> 48:15.476
[professor] Visiting neurology resident
from Boston General Hospital,

48:15.559 --> 48:16.727
Cha Sujin.

48:17.269 --> 48:18.479
I'm Cha Sujin.

48:18.562 --> 48:20.648
I'll do my best
to learn as much as I can here.

48:20.731 --> 48:22.525
-Nice to meet you all.
-[applause]

48:27.530 --> 48:28.697
[doctor] Dr. Cha.

48:28.781 --> 48:30.282
You shouldn't wear accessories here.

48:30.366 --> 48:33.619
Sorry. I forgot to take it off.

48:35.121 --> 48:37.498
MEDICAL STAFF SEARCH

48:37.581 --> 48:40.459
LEE SUJIN

48:41.627 --> 48:43.421
[Chan] I'm sure she was in a gown.

48:45.339 --> 48:48.175
[breathes deeply]

48:50.428 --> 48:51.429
[♪ music fades]

48:51.512 --> 48:52.513
All right.

48:53.139 --> 48:54.849
I got the results. [chuckles]

48:54.932 --> 48:58.269
-[inhales deeply]
-But why did you suddenly get off earlier?

48:58.978 --> 49:00.896
Oh. It was nothing.

49:00.980 --> 49:02.606
There's a convenience store nearby.

49:02.690 --> 49:04.358
I'll go buy some drinks for the nurses.

49:04.442 --> 49:05.943
-[Manjae] Mmm.
-[plastic rustling]

49:06.902 --> 49:09.071
Hmm? They didn't say it was going to rain.

49:09.530 --> 49:10.614
Is it a shower?

49:10.698 --> 49:12.908
I have a hood, so it's fine.
I'll be back soon.

49:12.992 --> 49:14.326
[Manjae] Okay.

49:15.995 --> 49:18.038
[♪ mysterious music playing]

49:19.915 --> 49:21.959
[Sujin] Who's that? Your friend?

49:22.042 --> 49:23.711
[Hyeokchan] No, just my roommate.

49:27.173 --> 49:29.925
Dr. Cha, we're starting rounds.

49:30.551 --> 49:31.552
[Sujin] Okay.

49:34.722 --> 49:35.806
[Haran] Hospitalized?

49:36.515 --> 49:38.642
-Hyeokchan?
-[Eunchan] Don't you remember?

49:39.226 --> 49:41.645
He hurt his hand badly in the lab.

49:41.729 --> 49:42.980
He even got surgery.

49:43.939 --> 49:45.024
A surgery?

49:45.816 --> 49:48.360
I never heard anything about that.

49:48.444 --> 49:49.445
[♪ music fades]

49:49.528 --> 49:51.363
-[Nana exclaims excitedly]
-[Manjae chuckles]

49:51.447 --> 49:52.781
Manjae, what do you think?

49:52.865 --> 49:55.784
[exclaims] It looks like
Genius' paw print. It's cute.

49:55.868 --> 49:57.328
-Right?
-Should I buy it for you?

49:57.411 --> 49:59.455
-Sure.
-Okay. How much is it?

49:59.538 --> 50:00.831
-Manjae!
-What? What is it?

50:00.915 --> 50:02.124
Tteokbokki! Tteokbokki!

50:02.208 --> 50:04.335
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

50:06.712 --> 50:08.464
[hums delightedly]

50:08.547 --> 50:10.382
[chuckles] It's good.

50:11.008 --> 50:14.136
Having tteokbokki after ditching
is the best.

50:14.220 --> 50:15.221
Right?

50:15.304 --> 50:17.973
That only applies
to the Chuncheon fashionista Nabong.

50:18.057 --> 50:20.184
I never ditched school.

50:20.809 --> 50:23.521
Ah. Right, of course.

50:23.604 --> 50:26.857
You were the bookworm Park Manjae.

50:26.941 --> 50:28.609
That's right.

50:28.692 --> 50:29.693
[both laugh]

50:30.277 --> 50:31.320
Excuse me.

50:31.862 --> 50:34.323
Are you Kim Nana, by any chance?

50:34.406 --> 50:35.616
It seems like it, right?

50:35.699 --> 50:37.535
We're fashion design majors,

50:37.618 --> 50:39.870
and we're huge fans.

50:39.954 --> 50:41.830
Could I have an autograph?

50:41.914 --> 50:45.209
Mmm… Oh, dear. My face is my autograph.

50:45.292 --> 50:47.586
You can take a selfie with me.

50:47.670 --> 50:50.172
-One, two, three.
-[camera clicks]

50:50.923 --> 50:53.050
[student 1] Thank you.

50:53.133 --> 50:56.136
By the way, your husband is freaking…

50:56.220 --> 50:58.055
[student 2] I mean, he's really cool.

50:58.138 --> 51:00.057
-No, I'm…
-He's freaking cool, isn't he?

51:00.683 --> 51:02.935
I care about looks.

51:03.018 --> 51:05.145
[students and Nana laugh]

51:08.774 --> 51:09.775
[♪ music fades]

51:13.028 --> 51:15.322
[Hayeong] Why do I feel so nervous
being alone with him?

51:15.406 --> 51:17.157
Oh… I feel so hot.

51:17.241 --> 51:20.286
Should I turn off the heater?
Would it show that I'm nervous?

51:20.369 --> 51:22.621
-[window whirring]
-[groans] It's hot.

51:22.705 --> 51:24.123
[breathes deeply]

51:26.250 --> 51:27.543
[coughing]

51:27.626 --> 51:28.961
[sniffles, clears throat]

51:29.420 --> 51:30.504
Should I close the window?

51:31.130 --> 51:32.965
No, it's fine. You can do as you like.

51:35.718 --> 51:37.261
[whirring]

51:42.308 --> 51:44.852
Then would it be possible to get samples?

51:44.935 --> 51:48.272
Yes, but it's over five times
the price of silk,

51:48.355 --> 51:50.274
and the durability tests
aren't stable yet.

51:50.357 --> 51:52.568
That's why I want to try this.

51:53.110 --> 51:54.278
I want to make clothes

51:54.361 --> 51:56.530
not just for display
but to prove the future.

51:56.989 --> 51:59.658
I really want to achieve that
for our brand.

51:59.742 --> 52:01.535
You seem very determined.

52:01.619 --> 52:03.871
How should we get the samples?

52:03.954 --> 52:06.206
There's a research facility
I came in touch with.

52:06.290 --> 52:08.917
It's a bio startup company.
I'll give you their number.

52:09.460 --> 52:10.753
-Really?
-[reporter] Yes.

52:11.253 --> 52:15.049
And I'll ask them again
for their cooperation.

52:15.132 --> 52:17.009
Thank you… [groans, chuckles excitedly]

52:17.092 --> 52:18.218
I was just so grateful.

52:18.302 --> 52:20.638
-Are you all right? [laughs]
-[Hayeong] Yes.

52:20.721 --> 52:22.640
-You really mean it?
-Of course.

52:22.723 --> 52:24.725
-Ms. Song, here's my business card.
-Ah.

52:24.808 --> 52:26.518
Contact me if you have any questions.

52:26.602 --> 52:27.728
Thank you.

52:27.811 --> 52:29.355
It was nice seeing you again, Taeseok.

52:29.438 --> 52:32.358
What? Do you two know each other?

52:32.441 --> 52:33.776
Why didn't you tell me?

52:34.360 --> 52:37.363
I'm actually his junior from college.

52:37.446 --> 52:38.572
He asked me

52:38.656 --> 52:40.616
to keep it a secret
in case you felt uneasy.

52:41.450 --> 52:44.495
I tried to get close to him,
but he never let me back then.

52:44.953 --> 52:45.996
And now--

52:46.080 --> 52:48.082
Thank you for today, Mr. Chae.

52:48.165 --> 52:49.416
I'll see you next time.

52:49.958 --> 52:51.168
You haven't changed a bit.

52:53.170 --> 52:56.548
I'd like to get to know you better.

52:56.632 --> 52:58.842
How about a glass of wine together?

52:59.468 --> 53:00.844
Just the two of us.

53:01.345 --> 53:04.556
Just the two of us?

53:05.140 --> 53:06.141
That's okay, right?

53:06.975 --> 53:09.144
I don't think it's my place
to say yes or no.

53:10.062 --> 53:11.063
Then excuse me.

53:13.941 --> 53:15.484
[Hayeong] What was that?

53:15.567 --> 53:17.611
Did he just set me up on a date?

53:18.028 --> 53:19.613
Didn't he have feelings for me?

53:20.906 --> 53:21.990
Mr. Yeon.

53:22.533 --> 53:25.577
Is it really okay for me
to have a drink with him, alone?

53:26.203 --> 53:28.122
Why are you asking me that?

53:28.205 --> 53:30.165
I think it's your business.

53:30.249 --> 53:31.583
[♪ whimsical music playing]

53:31.667 --> 53:33.419
Ah. Fine.

53:37.297 --> 53:39.925
Mr. Chae, let's go have some wine.

53:40.008 --> 53:41.760
I'm really craving a drink today.

53:47.057 --> 53:48.058
[sighs]

53:49.518 --> 53:50.936
-[sighs]
-[♪ music fades]

53:51.478 --> 53:53.731
[Yougyum's mom] Hadam, enjoy these dishes.

53:53.814 --> 53:56.483
You even packed side dishes for me?

53:56.567 --> 53:57.735
Thank you.

53:57.818 --> 53:59.695
Make sure to visit after the CSAT.

53:59.778 --> 54:01.238
I promise I will.

54:02.281 --> 54:05.075
But could you give me

54:06.577 --> 54:07.911
one more hug?

54:07.995 --> 54:10.247
Of course, I can. Come here.

54:10.330 --> 54:11.331
[chuckles]

54:11.415 --> 54:12.875
-[♪ amusing music playing]
-[Yougyum's mom exclaims]

54:12.958 --> 54:14.835
I'll see you again later. Hmm?

54:14.918 --> 54:15.961
Okay.

54:16.044 --> 54:18.505
-Me too. I want a hug, too.
-My goodness!

54:18.589 --> 54:21.049
[exclaims] Then I should join as well.

54:21.133 --> 54:24.219
[all laughing]

54:25.721 --> 54:29.224
[Haran] A surgery?
I never heard anything about that.

54:29.308 --> 54:30.768
[Eunchan] You didn't know?

54:31.435 --> 54:34.730
I guess Chan didn't tell you
in case you got worried.

54:39.318 --> 54:41.695
[Chan clears throat] Excuse me.

54:41.779 --> 54:46.116
You're Designer Song Haran
who won the Best Designer Award, right?

54:46.950 --> 54:49.119
[chuckles] Oh? How are you here?

54:49.203 --> 54:52.122
I have a habit of congratulating people
who receive awards.

54:52.998 --> 54:54.291
Here.

54:54.791 --> 54:55.792
Congratulations.

54:55.876 --> 54:57.586
[♪ uplifting song playing]

54:58.420 --> 54:59.463
Thanks.

55:00.547 --> 55:03.634
[inhales sharply]
But why do you look so down

55:04.218 --> 55:05.594
when you just won an award?

55:06.261 --> 55:08.263
No, I'm really happy.

55:08.347 --> 55:10.474
No, your expression looks…

55:11.975 --> 55:13.727
-like this.
-[chuckles]

55:14.436 --> 55:16.855
[chuckles softly] Let's go.

55:16.939 --> 55:18.106
Go where?

55:18.899 --> 55:20.692
Photos? That's so random.

55:21.527 --> 55:23.237
I told you, what you took doesn't count.

55:23.320 --> 55:24.863
Oh. This one's good.

55:24.947 --> 55:26.281
All right. Come here.

55:29.993 --> 55:32.162
Our Best Designer.

55:34.498 --> 55:36.917
Okay. One, two, three.

55:39.419 --> 55:40.587
You should smile.

55:41.421 --> 55:42.673
This time with the flowers.

55:42.756 --> 55:43.757
Here. Smile.

55:45.342 --> 55:47.386
All right. One, two, three.

55:48.303 --> 55:51.098
I'll do an ugly face for you
to make you look prettier.

55:51.181 --> 55:53.141
One, two, three. [hums teasingly]

55:54.476 --> 55:55.561
[Haran chuckles]

55:55.644 --> 55:56.645
[Chan chuckles]

55:57.354 --> 55:59.064
Pretty pose. [sneezes]

56:00.440 --> 56:02.484
[Haran] Look at your expressions.
[giggles]

56:05.153 --> 56:07.072
-Let's go to our next course.
-What?

56:07.155 --> 56:09.241
Where? Where are we going?

56:10.701 --> 56:12.369
Come on, let's go.

56:13.161 --> 56:14.162
This way.

56:17.416 --> 56:20.544
Wow. You came to such
a nice place alone? Tsk.

56:21.086 --> 56:23.171
You're the one
who disappeared without telling me.

56:25.632 --> 56:27.926
Excuse me, could you take a picture of us?

56:28.010 --> 56:29.761
Sure, of course.

56:29.845 --> 56:31.722
-Two, three.
-[camera clicks]

56:32.306 --> 56:34.266
-Thank you.
-[Chan] Thank you.

56:34.349 --> 56:36.310
Would you like a photo, too?

56:37.519 --> 56:38.770
Sure.

56:38.854 --> 56:41.315
Okay. Smile. [clears throat]

56:41.398 --> 56:43.358
It'll look nice
if you smile at each other.

56:43.442 --> 56:45.485
-Can you look at each other?
-Like this?

56:49.615 --> 56:51.199
What should I do?

56:52.075 --> 56:54.411
-[Chan] I'll do an ugly face for you.
-[chuckles]

56:54.494 --> 56:56.663
-We'll take one for you, too.
-Oh, I'm okay.

57:01.918 --> 57:03.128
[mouthing] Thank you.

57:05.714 --> 57:07.090
[man] I'll take it now.

57:07.174 --> 57:09.092
One, two, three.

57:13.555 --> 57:14.556
[♪ song fades]

57:15.474 --> 57:18.727
[Hadam] There's a blanket I've been using
since I was a baby,

57:19.645 --> 57:21.688
and it had this distinctive scent.

57:23.523 --> 57:27.027
It felt warm and comforting

57:28.779 --> 57:30.947
and made me feel like I'm going to cry.

57:33.533 --> 57:35.661
But that scent disappeared.

57:36.328 --> 57:38.538
It smelled just like my mom used to.

57:40.415 --> 57:42.334
But when your mom hugged me earlier,

57:44.753 --> 57:45.921
I smelled the same scent.

57:46.004 --> 57:48.173
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

57:50.967 --> 57:51.968
[chuckles softly]

57:53.261 --> 57:54.471
So I ended up crying.

57:56.139 --> 57:58.225
I thought it was the smell of detergent,

57:59.434 --> 58:01.103
but I guess that was the scent of a mom.

58:03.939 --> 58:06.441
Oh? Then wouldn't I smell similar?

58:07.734 --> 58:08.735
Try smelling me.

58:10.696 --> 58:11.947
[Hadam sniffs]

58:12.030 --> 58:14.157
[both laugh]

58:14.241 --> 58:16.326
You have a different scent.

58:18.078 --> 58:20.580
I'm going to marry you, no matter what.

58:20.664 --> 58:21.707
What?

58:21.790 --> 58:23.959
[chuckles] Whenever I see you,

58:24.042 --> 58:27.003
I wonder how you could be so wonderful.

58:27.087 --> 58:29.089
But I understood when I saw your parents.

58:29.673 --> 58:31.967
If they become my family,

58:32.551 --> 58:34.177
I'll be so happy.

58:36.221 --> 58:38.014
Still, I'll love you the most.

58:39.599 --> 58:40.642
What do I do?

58:41.268 --> 58:44.730
[sighs] I'm so happy,
I feel like I'm going to faint.

58:44.813 --> 58:48.024
[chuckles] There's nothing left
but happiness for us.

58:48.108 --> 58:49.234
Mm.

58:50.402 --> 58:52.612
Let's go. I want to study.

58:52.696 --> 58:53.947
Okay.

58:55.073 --> 58:56.408
The minimum CSAT requirement?

58:57.117 --> 58:59.077
It's going to be a piece of cake.

59:02.664 --> 59:03.957
Why aren't you coming?

59:04.040 --> 59:05.667
-[♪ music fades]
-[Hadam giggles]

59:05.751 --> 59:07.377
Did you really faint?

59:08.462 --> 59:10.922
Come on. Stop fooling around.

59:12.591 --> 59:14.968
[breath trembling] Hadam, what do I do?

59:18.180 --> 59:20.474
I can't get up.

59:21.057 --> 59:22.058
My foot…

59:22.142 --> 59:23.143
What?

59:23.226 --> 59:25.228
[♪ tense music playing]

59:27.564 --> 59:29.316
-[winces]
-Huh?

59:36.948 --> 59:37.949
[stutters] Yougyum…

59:38.033 --> 59:39.034
[♪ music fades]

59:39.618 --> 59:41.119
Thank you for the umbrella.

59:41.203 --> 59:42.329
[both chuckle]

59:44.122 --> 59:45.582
See you.

59:46.291 --> 59:47.417
-[in English] Yes!
-[in Korean] Bye.

59:47.501 --> 59:48.585
Sure. Bye.

59:48.668 --> 59:49.878
-Bye.
-Get home safely.

59:49.961 --> 59:50.962
Okay.

59:52.506 --> 59:56.259
Tsk. He made me
get my hopes up for nothing.

59:58.553 --> 01:00:00.806
I should thank him.

01:00:01.389 --> 01:00:04.935
I'm so grateful that he introduced us.

01:00:07.103 --> 01:00:09.105
[line connects, rings]

01:00:09.981 --> 01:00:11.107
Why isn't he picking up?

01:00:16.696 --> 01:00:20.867
Mr. Yeon, I had so much fun
with Mr. Chae today…

01:00:22.536 --> 01:00:23.745
What are you spying on?

01:00:23.829 --> 01:00:25.580
Gosh, you scared me.

01:00:26.581 --> 01:00:29.584
Did Mr. Yeon not come back here
after the meeting?

01:00:29.668 --> 01:00:31.461
He just dropped by for a bit and left.

01:00:32.128 --> 01:00:33.129
Ah.

01:00:33.213 --> 01:00:34.381
You'd better buy me lunch…

01:00:34.840 --> 01:00:37.384
[in singsong] for the information.

01:00:38.844 --> 01:00:41.012
He always gets off work late, though.

01:00:41.096 --> 01:00:42.305
[deliveryman] Mr. Yeon Taeseok?

01:00:43.515 --> 01:00:44.891
There's a delivery for you.

01:00:45.559 --> 01:00:47.227
I'll take that.

01:00:47.310 --> 01:00:48.854
Thank you.

01:00:48.937 --> 01:00:51.022
YEON TAESEOK

01:00:57.863 --> 01:00:59.531
Mr. Yeon.

01:01:04.411 --> 01:01:06.496
What? He's not home, either?

01:01:10.917 --> 01:01:12.752
Mr. Yeon, I…

01:01:14.004 --> 01:01:15.005
Oh?

01:01:15.088 --> 01:01:17.340
[♪ somber music playing]

01:01:17.424 --> 01:01:18.633
What…

01:01:18.717 --> 01:01:20.302
-What's going on?
-[breath trembling]

01:01:22.345 --> 01:01:23.346
[♪ music fades]

01:01:23.930 --> 01:01:27.767
[exclaims delightedly]
This keychain is so cute. [chuckles]

01:01:28.268 --> 01:01:30.979
Manjae, let's go have sujebi next time.

01:01:32.397 --> 01:01:35.442
And let's visit Chuncheon as well
before it gets colder.

01:01:35.525 --> 01:01:36.985
-Let's…
-Kim Nabong.

01:01:38.320 --> 01:01:39.362
What?

01:01:39.446 --> 01:01:40.447
Why aren't you coming?

01:01:41.781 --> 01:01:42.866
You.

01:01:45.201 --> 01:01:46.578
Where are you going this time?

01:01:47.203 --> 01:01:48.538
I said let's go to Chuncheon.

01:01:48.622 --> 01:01:50.957
You're behaving just like back then.

01:01:51.041 --> 01:01:53.835
When you suddenly left for France
when you were 20,

01:01:53.919 --> 01:01:55.128
you acted just like this.

01:01:55.211 --> 01:01:57.756
You called me out of the blue

01:01:57.839 --> 01:02:00.216
and said, "Let's do this. Let's go here."

01:02:00.967 --> 01:02:03.845
Then you suddenly disappeared
without saying anything.

01:02:03.929 --> 01:02:05.972
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:02:06.932 --> 01:02:09.768
That was a long time ago. Don't be silly.

01:02:09.851 --> 01:02:10.894
Tell me.

01:02:11.728 --> 01:02:13.021
What is it this time?

01:02:13.480 --> 01:02:15.231
What on earth is going on with you?

01:02:19.736 --> 01:02:21.112
[Haran chuckles softly]

01:02:22.697 --> 01:02:24.699
[cell phone vibrating]

01:02:30.664 --> 01:02:31.790
Hello?

01:02:33.500 --> 01:02:35.627
Yes. May I ask who's calling?

01:02:44.636 --> 01:02:45.804
Oh…

01:02:45.887 --> 01:02:47.138
All right.

01:02:47.222 --> 01:02:48.723
I'll go and check.

01:02:57.565 --> 01:02:58.566
[♪ music fades]

01:02:58.650 --> 01:03:00.694
[grunts, inhales sharply] Ah.

01:03:02.946 --> 01:03:04.072
[hums]

01:03:06.741 --> 01:03:09.703
[sighs] I miss you already.

01:03:10.704 --> 01:03:11.705
[chuckles softly]

01:03:12.414 --> 01:03:14.290
[cell phone buzzes, chimes]

01:03:14.374 --> 01:03:16.501
-Hmm?
-[Haran] Can you come out for a bit?

01:03:22.841 --> 01:03:25.343
[pants] That was fast, wasn't it?

01:03:25.844 --> 01:03:26.886
Aren't you tired?

01:03:27.387 --> 01:03:29.848
I mean, I told you to go home and rest,

01:03:29.931 --> 01:03:30.932
but…

01:03:31.641 --> 01:03:35.812
I was actually really sad
that you left. [chuckles]

01:03:35.895 --> 01:03:38.189
[♪ tense music playing]

01:03:38.815 --> 01:03:39.816
What is it?

01:03:40.483 --> 01:03:41.735
Is something wrong?

01:03:42.569 --> 01:03:45.613
I just got a call from the restaurant.

01:03:45.697 --> 01:03:47.157
What restaurant?

01:03:52.871 --> 01:03:54.873
[♪ music intensifies]

01:04:00.962 --> 01:04:03.965
I think you owe me an explanation.

01:04:07.343 --> 01:04:09.596
[high-pitched ringing]

01:04:25.779 --> 01:04:26.780
[♪ music fades]

01:04:29.074 --> 01:04:31.034
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:04:31.117 --> 01:04:33.119
[♪ emotional song playing]

01:04:55.141 --> 01:04:59.646
[Haran] It sounds like
they're not meant to be together.

01:04:59.729 --> 01:05:03.233
[Chan] Can you tell me what you know
about what happened seven years ago?

01:05:03.316 --> 01:05:05.485
I'll tell her everything

01:05:05.568 --> 01:05:08.196
and apologize to her.

01:05:08.279 --> 01:05:12.575
[Taeseok] The chance
of Ms. Song and I dating is zero.

01:05:12.659 --> 01:05:17.288
[Hayeong] Am I really just mistaken
about all those situations?

01:05:17.372 --> 01:05:19.874
[Nana] It's rare to find
someone who makes you smile.

01:05:19.958 --> 01:05:21.918
[Haran crying] What if you're not okay?

01:05:22.001 --> 01:05:23.545
What if something else happens?

01:05:23.628 --> 01:05:26.131
[Chan] I want to stay by her side,

01:05:26.214 --> 01:05:28.007
but I don't know what to do.

01:05:31.386 --> 01:05:32.387
[♪ song fades]

01:05:32.470 --> 01:05:34.472
[♪ theme music playing]

01:05:40.353 --> 01:05:41.354
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:05:41.437 --> 01:05:42.438
Translated by Juyoung Park
